# Backend Rules

Stack:
- Node.js
- Express
- MongoDB
- JWT Authentication

Rules:

- Validate all request bodies
- Use middleware for auth and permissions
- Never trust frontend data
- Use proper HTTP status codes
- Separate routes/controllers/services
- Add centralized error handling
- Avoid callback hell
- Use async/await only
- Protect sensitive routes
- Add logging system
- Prevent duplicated Mongo queries
- Optimize indexes
- Add pagination everywhere needed
- Validate GPS/location data
- Handle reconnection events
- Create robust alert persistence
- Ensure all endpoints return predictable JSON
